== Shrine Grounds ==
=== Main Shrine ===
The shrine comprises a haiden, heiden, and a covered three-bay honden in {{ill|Miya-zukuri|ja|流造|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Miya-zukuri|qq=}} style. The honden features three doors, symbolizing the deities enshrined. Presently, the shrine honors two deities, with one seat left vacant.

<gallery widths="200px" heights="150px">
File:Honden of Unakorowake-jinja 1.JPG|Honden (Three-bay miya-zukuri style)
File:Unakorowake-jinja 1.JPG|Haiden
</gallery>

=== Torii and Approach ===
A stream flows beneath the torii. The approach features memorial stones, subsidiary shrines, and a shrine office.

<gallery>
File:Suitengu shrine of Unakorowake-jinja.JPG|Water deity shrine
File:Main approach to Unakorowake-jinja 2.JPG|Main approach
File:Torii gate of Unakorowake-jinja.JPG|Torii
</gallery>

=== Subsidiary Shrines ===
The shrine precinct includes various stone shrines dedicated to deities such as {{ill|Mishima Taisha|ja|三嶋神社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Mishima Taisha|qq=}}, {{ill|Izu-san Shrine|ja|伊豆山神社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Izu-san Shrine|qq=}}, {{ill|Hakone Shrine|ja|箱根神社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hakone Shrine|qq=}}, and others.

== Festivals ==
The Spring Festival is held annually from {{ill|April 2|ja|4月2日|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/April 2|qq=}}, and the Autumn Festival occurs from {{ill|September 18|ja|9月18日|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/September 18|qq=}}. Historical records indicate that events such as horseback archery were once part of the celebrations.

