'''Unakorowake Shrine''' (宇奈己呂和気神社) is a {{ill|Shinto shrine|ja|神社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shinto shrine|qq=}} located in {{ill|Kōriyama|ja|郡山市|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kōriyama|qq=}}, {{ill|Fukushima Prefecture|ja|福島県|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fukushima Prefecture|qq=}}. It is a {{ill|Shikinai shrine|ja|式内社|1=Shikinaisha|2=ja|3=式内社|qq=draft|1=Shikinaisha|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinai shrine|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinaisha|qq=}} ({{ill|Myōjin taisha|ja|名神大社|fr|Myōjin Taisha|zh|名神大社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Myōjin taisha|qq=}}), and its former shrine Ranking under the {{ill|Modern system of Ranked Shinto shrines|ja|近代社格制度|1=Modern system of ranked Shinto shrines|1=Modern system of Ranked Shinto shrines|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Modern system of Ranked Shinto shrines|13=User:Immanuelle/Modern system of ranked Shinto shrines|qq=}} was {{ill|Gōsha|ja|郷社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Gōsha|qq=}}.
[[Unakoro Waki Shrine]] is a regional [[Sōja shrine|Sōja shrine]]. It enshrines many kami of the local region.

It contrasts with provincial Soja shrines which enshrine all the kami of a province<ref>https://archive.ph/wip/XtZfZ</ref>

== Enshrined Deities ==
'''Main deity'''
* '''{{ill|Seoritsu-Hime|lt=Seoritsu-Hime|lt=Seoritsuhime|ja|瀬織津比売命|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Seoritsuhime|qq=}}''' - One of the {{ill|Haraedo no Kami|lt=Haraedo no Kami|lt=Haraedo-no-Ōkami|ja|祓戸大神|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Haraedo-no-Ōkami|qq=}}

'''Secondary deity'''
* {{ill|Hachiman|ja|八幡神|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hachiman|qq=}}: Hondawake-no-Mikoto ({{ill|Emperor Ōjin|ja|応神天皇|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Emperor Ōjin|qq=}})

== History ==
=== Founding ===
According to ancient records, during the reign of {{ill|Emperor Kōnin|ja|光仁天皇|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Emperor Kōnin|qq=}}, disturbances caused by the {{ill|Emishi|ja|蝦夷|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Emishi|qq=}} were widespread in the Mutsu Province. In the first year of {{ill|Ten'ō|ja|天応|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ten'ō|qq=}} ({{ill|781|ja|781年|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/781|qq=}}), the court dispatched {{ill|Fujiwara no Oguro|ja|藤原小黒麿|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fujiwara no Oguro|qq=}} as inspector of Mutsu and Dewa, but he failed to suppress the unrest. The following year, in the first year of {{ill|Enryaku|ja|延暦|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Enryaku|qq=}} ({{ill|782|ja|782年|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/782|qq=}}), the newly enthroned {{ill|Emperor Kanmu|ja|桓武天皇|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Emperor Kanmu|qq=}} sent {{ill|Ōtomo no Yakamochi|ja|大伴家持|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōtomo no Yakamochi|qq=}} to the region as an inspector and commander. After seeking divine guidance on {{ill|Takahatayama|ja|高旗山|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Takahatayama|qq=}}, Yakamochi established a shrine to enshrine Seoritsuhime, whose divine power reportedly aided in subduing the unrest.

Later, in the 3rd year of Enryaku ({{ill|784|ja|784年|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/784|qq=}}), the shrine was moved from Takahatayama to its current location in Yamazaki. At that time, {{ill|Hachiman|ja|八幡大神|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hachiman|qq=}} (Hondawake-no-Mikoto) was enshrined as a secondary deity. A stone shrine (okumiya) remains on the summit of Takahatayama, and an information board at the mountain trailhead near {{ill|Genda Onsen|ja|源田温泉|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Genda Onsen|qq=}} recounts this history.

According to shrine records, the shrine’s origins trace back to the 11th year of Emperor Kinmei ({{ill|550|ja|550年|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/550|qq=}}?). During that time, Seoritsuhime was believed to have manifested on Takahatayama's summit. Seoritsuhime, identified as a deity born from the purification of {{ill|Izanagi|ja|伊耶那岐命|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Izanagi|qq=}} at Awagihara, was venerated for her ability to cleanse impurities and pacify disturbances. 

=== Historical Overview ===
As recorded in the {{ill|Shoku Nihongi|ja|続日本後紀|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shoku Nihongi|qq=}}, the shrine was granted the Rank of Junior Fifth Rank, Lower Grade, in the 14th year of {{ill|Jōwa (Heian period)|ja|承和|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Jōwa (Heian period)|qq=}} ({{ill|847|ja|847年|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/847|qq=}}). According to the {{ill|Ruijū Kokushi|ja|類聚国史|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ruijū Kokushi|qq=}}, the shrine's Rank was elevated to Senior Fifth Rank, Lower Grade, in the 11th year of {{ill|Jōgan|ja|貞観|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Jōgan|qq=}} ({{ill|869|ja|869年|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/869|qq=}}).

In {{ill|927|ja|927年|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/927|qq=}}, the shrine was listed as a {{ill|Myōjin taisha|ja|名神大社|fr|Myōjin Taisha|zh|名神大社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Myōjin taisha|qq=}} in the {{ill|Engishiki|ja|延喜式|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Engishiki|qq=}} and became the main shrine of the three {{ill|Shikinaisha|ja|式内社|1=Shikinaisha|2=ja|3=式内社|qq=draft|1=Shikinaisha|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinaisha|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinaisha|qq=}} in the Asaka District, receiving deep veneration from both rulers and local residents. It was also designated the total shrine (sōsha) for the {{ill|33 communities of Asaka|ja|安積三十三郷|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/33 communities of Asaka|qq=}}.

During the {{ill|Kamakura period|ja|鎌倉時代|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kamakura period|qq=}}, {{ill|Kudō Suketsune|ja|工藤祐経|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kudō Suketsune|qq=}}, appointed as local governor, introduced deities from the {{ill|Mishima Taisha|ja|三嶋大社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Mishima Taisha|qq=}} and other shrines in Izu Province as subordinate shrines. The shrine was further restored by local rulers such as {{ill|Ashina clan|ja|蘆名氏|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ashina clan|qq=}} and {{ill|Gamo Ujisato|ja|蒲生氏郷|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Gamo Ujisato|qq=}}, and it received land grants and other support.

=== typeings ===
* {{ill|Jōwa (Heian period)|ja|承和|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Jōwa (Heian period)|qq=}} 14 ({{ill|847|ja|847年|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/847|qq=}}): Junior Fifth Rank, Lower Grade ({{ill|Shoku Nihongi|ja|続日本後紀|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shoku Nihongi|qq=}})
