== Auxiliary and subordinate shrines ==
To the west of the main shrine building lies the '''Yōsan Shrine''' (dedicated to Uka-no-Mitama-no-Kami and Wakumusubi-no-Kami) and a memorial shrine for the war dead. Additional stone shrines enshrine deities such as Mishima Shrine, Izusan Shrine, Hakone Shrine (all brought by Kudō Suketsune), Aosa Shrine, Yama Shrine, Inari Shrine, Kasuga Shrine, Tenman-gū, Itsukushima Shrine, and others.

== Festivals ==
The spring grand festival takes place from April 2 to April 4, and the autumn grand festival occurs from September 18 to September 20. In the past, events such as yabusame (horseback archery) and mikoshi processions were held but were discontinued following the {{ill|Kakitsu Rebellion|ja|嘉吉の乱|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kakitsu Rebellion|1=Kakitsu incident|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q5365139}} in 1441 and the {{ill|Kanshō famine|en|Kanshō famine|WD=Q11653527|lt=Great Famine of Chōroku and Kanshō|1=Kanshō famine}} in 1459. While attempts were made to revive the mikoshi processions under the protection of the Tanba clan during the Edo period, these rituals are no longer performed.

== Access ==
'''location'''
* 76 Kamino-dai, Hachiman, Mihota-machi, Kōriyama City, Fukushima Prefecture, Japan.

=== By bus ===
* From {{ill|Kōriyama Station (Fukushima)|en|Kōriyama Station (Fukushima)|WD=Q385879|lt=Koriyama Station (Fukushima)|1=Kōriyama Station (Fukushima)}} (JR East Tōhoku Shinkansen), take the No. 2 bus bound for Naganuma (approx. 35 minutes) and alight at "Mihota Public Hall." The shrine is a short walk away. Check timetables for details.

=== By car ===
* About 10 minutes from {{ill|Kōriyama Minami Interchange (Fukushima)|ja|郡山南インターチェンジ (福島県)|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kōriyama Minami Interchange (Fukushima)|1=Koriyama-minami interchange|comment=changed title based on wikidata|WD=Q11643156}}.

